    "reasoning_content": "PDFs are raw binary. I'll rely on websearch for facts about the Voyager 25M in-silico screen and Bryant/Kelsic ML paper. The PMC11381518 fetch gave good content: AlphaFold-Multimer \"5 structural models each of X1 and CAP-Mac peptides with up to 20 recycles\" — that's a concrete compute quantity! \"Representative AlphaFold models, from 5 structural models each of X1 and CAP-Mac peptides with up to 20 recycles\" — great for compute_open on structure-matrix option: largest reported = 5 models × 20 recycles per peptide pair (source PMC11381518). And unknown above: whether more seeds/recycles/complexes would make receptor-class geometry predictive of sorting fate.\n\nAlso the Retrogenix screen: >6400 proteins (6019 human plasma membrane + secreted + 397 heterodimers), >90% of human membrane proteome — good.\n\nNow let me search for:\n1. Voyager 25M in silico sequences (Cox ASGCT 2025).\n2. Bryant Kelsic ML 2021 AAV (Nature Biotechnology?) — \"Deep diversification of an AAV capsid protein by machine learning\"? Actually I recall the paper: Bryant DH, Kelsic ED, et al. \"Deep diversification of an AAV capsid protein by machine learning\" Nature Biotechnology 2021. Let me search.\n3. GPU MD throughput / sequential MD steps; replica-parallel MD.\n4. AlphaFold DB 200M+ / large scale structure prediction pipelines.\n5. AAV9 pH 5.5 galactose MD (jvi.00843-21) — details of MD (length etc.).\n\nLet me do web searches."
